RepriceService:

```php
final class RepriceService
{
    public function __construct(private EntityManagerInterface $em, private CostCalculator $calculator) {}

    /** @return array{events:int, delta:string} */
    public function reprice(PriceFile $file): array
    {
        $affectedRowIds = [];
        $this->em->transactional(function () use ($file, &$affectedRowIds) {
            // 1) discover which existing price rows will actually change
            foreach ($file->getPrices() as $spec) {
                $model = $this->lookupModel($spec->getProviderCode(), $spec->getModel());
                if ($model === null) continue; // validation/importer raises
                $row = $this->findRowByModelTs($model->getId(), $spec->getValidFrom());
                if ($row !== null && !$spec->sameContent([unit, currency, rates])) $affectedRowIds[] = $row->getId();
            }
            // 2) apply the upsert (reuse PriceImporter)
            $this->importer->import($file);

            // 3) recomputation of the affected rated events
            $delta = '0'; $count = 0;
            foreach (array_unique($affectedRowIds) as $rowId) {
                $events = $em->getRepository(UsageEvent::class)->findBy(['priceRowId' => $rowId, 'status' => UsageEvent::STATUS_RATED]);
                foreach ($events as $e) {
                    $newRow = $em->find(PriceRow::class, $rowId);
                    $provider = $em->getRepository(Provider::class)->findOneBy(['code' => $e->getProvider()]);
                    $off = $provider?->getOffPeak();
                    $res = $this->calculator->calculate($newRow, $e->getTokens(), $off, $e->getTs());
                    $old = $e->getCostUsd();
                    $delta = Decimals::add($delta, Decimals::sub($res['costUsd'], $old));
                    $e->markRated($rowId, $res['baseCost'], $res['offPeakApplied'], $res['costUsd']);
                    $count++;
                }
            }
            $em->flush();
        });
        return ['events' => $count, 'delta' => $delta];
    }
}
```

Caveat: findBy(['priceRowId'...]) — the field name in DQL is priceRowId. Also caveat: findBy + the identity map is fine.

Edge case: event ts and the new row's valid_from... the re-calculation uses the same row (the one replaced) — by definition of the affected set the event was billed with that row (the row key is unchanged, only the rate changed). Correct.

Note: if the content of a row changed but the event was also billed with that row — no problem. If a row is *added* (it didn't exist), then no event will reference it. If a row existed and the content changed → recalculate.

Also: if the content changed but is identical → skip (avoid useless recalculation).

